  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize 'Five-Block' theory. Your hand should be visualized as 4 sets and 1 pair. If you have 6 potential blocks, discard the weakest one immediately to increase efficiency.\n\nYaku Awareness: Don't just pick up tiles. If you open your hand (call Chow/Pung), you lose the ability to declare Riichi. Only open your hand if you have a guaranteed Yaku like 'All Simples' or 'Dragon Pung'.\n\nDefensive Folding (Beta-Ori): If an opponent declares Riichi, stop trying to win. Discard 'Safe Tiles' (Genbutsu) that the opponent already discarded, as they cannot win on those due to the Furiten rule.",
